# Example denylist for the confidentiality gate (scripts/gate.mjs, ADR 0005).
# Format: one regular expression per line, matched case-insensitively, with ^ and $ per line.
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored. The #n in the gate output counts active patterns only.
# Start a local file with: cp -n .confidential-patterns.example .confidential-patterns
# The real file is gitignored and must never be committed. Every token below is invented.
#
# Each active pattern hides one character in a class, so it matches its token but not its own source line.

# A plain word.
vrelk[a]nthum

# An anchored pattern: matches only a line that is exactly the token.
^snorv[e]lt-quill$

# An invalid regular expression, kept commented out so a copy of this file passes the gate.
# Uncomment the next line to see the gate reject it.
# (unclosed[group
